  "configuration_id": "config_044",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best singleprofile result (config_016: pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + concat, acc=0.535) clearly outperforms rna_only (0.485) and image_only (0.208), and fusion method (concat vs weighted) makes negligible difference. However, all six completed experiments are singleprofile; we have zero evidence on whether multiprofile + aggregation can improve performance. Question: config_044 extends our best singleprofile configuration (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) to multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool), directly testing whether additional profiles add signal beyond what a single profile captures. Why this is the best next step: (1) It isolates the multiprofile/aggregation question while holding the proven-best encoders and fusion constant, avoiding confounds from simultaneously changing multiple variables. (2) Starting with avgpool (simpler than transformer) is more informative: if it helps, multiprofile is beneficial without complex aggregation; if it doesn't, we can then test whether transformer aggregation is specifically needed. (3) The potential upside is large—if multiprofile pushes accuracy meaningfully above 0.535, it opens a productive search direction; if it doesn't, we efficiently rule out that axis and refocus on encoder or fusion refinements."
}

